    {
      "title": "Body of the hat",
      "slug": "body-of-the-hat",
      "displayOrder": 3,
      "legacy": {
        "itemId": 706,
        "lessonOrder": 3
      },
      "blocks": [
        {
          "components": [
            {
              "type": "richText",
              "html": "Because hats are \"tubes\" it's important to plan stitch patterns to match at the seam.<br>If necessary, adjust the stitch count of your hat to accommodate your chosen stitch pattern",
              "legacyComponentId": 9157,
              "order": 1
            },
            {
              "type": "video",
              "vimeoId": "151857799",
              "title": "Stitch Multiples",
              "legacyComponentId": 9155,
              "order": 2
            },
            {
              "type": "richText",
              "html": "<style>\r\nhr.style13 {\r\nheight: 10px;\r\nborder: 0;\r\nbox-shadow: 0 10px 10px -10px #8c8b8b inset;\r\n}\r\n\r\n</style>\r\n\r\n<hr class=\"style13\">\r\n\r\n\r\n    \r\n\r\n<span class=\"handwriting\" style=\"font-size:2em\"> Need help with stitch patterning? </span><br><span class=\"yellow_highlight\"> Learn to knit in pattern in 3 steps</span><br>One of the many advantages of machine knitting is the ability to quickly and easily knit in pattern. Textured stitch patterns, multi-color patterns can all be quickly produced with the help of automatic patterning devices. Using Punchcard or electronics, the machine automatically selects needles for pattern knitting.<br>If you've been stumped by knitting in pattern on your machine, this course will take away the fear and confusion.<br>Using fill-in-the-blanks tutorials, we'll walk you through all the settings for YOUR machine, creating a cheat-sheet that you can use again and again.<br>Once you finish the exercises you will have an UNDERSTANDING of what is going on with all the levers and buttons and you will be confident to sit down and work the stitch pattern of your choice.\r\n    \r\n\r\n        <figure>\r\n            <a href=\"/challenge/72/automatic-stitch-patterning\"><img class=\"center-block\" src=\"/challenge/images/v2/109/v2/72/automatic_stitch.jpg\">\r\n            <figcaption align=\"center\"><br><i class=\"fa fa-hand-o-right\" aria-hidden=\"true\"></i> <b>Course: Automatic Stitch Patterning</b></figcaption>\r\n        </figure></a>\r\n    \r\n\r\n",
              "legacyComponentId": 9154,
              "order": 3
            }
          ],
          "title": "Stitch patterns",
          "slug": "stitch-patterns",
          "order": 1,
          "legacy": {
            "assignId": 6002,
            "blockType": "HTML"
          }
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "title": "Top shaping",
      "slug": "top-shaping",
      "displayOrder": 4,
      "legacy": {
        "itemId": 707,
        "lessonOrder": 4
      },
      "blocks": [
        {
          "components": [
            {
              "type": "richText",
              "html": "When knitting mile-a-minute hats, the quickest way to finish the \"tube\" is to run a tail of yarn through the last open stitches and gather the top of the Hat.\r\n\r\n",
              "legacyComponentId": 9142,
              "order": 1
            },
            {
              "type": "video",
              "vimeoId": "151859005",
              "title": "Gathered Top for Mittens and Hats",
              "legacyComponentId": 9143,
              "order": 2
            },
            {
              "type": "richText",
              "html": "<h2 id=\"lecture_heading\" class=\"section-title MachineknittingColor\"><i></i> Modified Gathers</h2> For reduced bulk at the top of the hat.\r\n\r\n\r\nApprox 2\" before the end of a basic hat (for adults):<br>\r\n<ol>\r\n<li>Rransfer every other needle to it's neighbor, leaving the emptied needles in out of work position.</li>\r\n<li>Leave at least 2 needles in work on the edges for seaming</li>\r\n<li>Knit 2\" of rows over every  other needle</li>\r\n<li>Gather top with live stitches</li>\r\n<li>Fasten tail and use for seaming<?li>\r\n</ol>\r\n\r\n<img src=\"/images/patterns/eon_gather.jpg\">\r\n\r\n\r\n",
              "legacyComponentId": 9160,
              "order": 3
            }
          ],
          "title": "Gathers",
          "slug": "gathers",
          "order": 1,
          "legacy": {
            "assignId": 6004,
            "blockType": "HTML"
          }
        },
        {
          "components": [
            {
              "type": "video",
              "vimeoId": "151858447",
              "title": "Basic Increasing and Decreasing",
              "legacySlot": 1,
              "legacyComponentId": 9144,
              "order": 1
            },
            {
              "type": "video",
              "vimeoId": "305566131",
              "title": "Shaped Crown Hat on the Machine",
              "legacySlot": 2,
              "legacyComponentId": 9144,
              "order": 1
            }
          ],
          "title": "Shaping",
          "slug": "shaping",
          "order": 2,
